"Le cedes la palabra. El vestuario lo agradece.":"You hand him the floor. The dressing room appreciates it.",
"Le confiesas que fue con la mano y anula el gol. Hasta los rivales te aplauden.":"You admit it was handball and he disallows the goal. Even the opposition applaud you.",
"Le contratas para llevar tus redes. Te ahorras disgustos.":"You hire him to run your social media. It saves you headaches.",
"Le convence el papel protagonista. ¡Fichado!":"The starring role convinces him. Signed!",
"Le dan otra temporada. Tu familia te lo agradece.":"They give him another season. Your family is grateful.",
"Le das con la espinilla. Saque de puerta.":"You hit it with your shin. Goal kick.",
"Le das el sí para verano. El vestuario se entera.":"You say yes for the summer. The dressing room finds out.",
"Le das las gracias, pero prefieres seguir tu propio camino.":"You thank him, but prefer to follow your own path.",
"Le das tu palabra al vestuario: os vais a quedar juntos hasta el final.":"You give the dressing room your word: you'll stay together to the end.",
"Le defiendes… y sigue sin dar una. La grada se impacienta.":"You defend him... and he still can't get anything right. The crowd grows impatient.",
"Le derribas de un cabezazo en el pecho. Roja directa y una imagen que dará la vuelta al mundo.":"You knock him down with a headbutt to the chest. Straight red and an image that will go around the world.",
"Le descolocas por completo.":"You completely throw him off.",
"Le deseo mucha suerte. La va a necesitar para la liga y para la vida. Y creo que me quedo corto.":"I wish him lots of luck. He'll need it for the league and for life. And I think that's an understatement.",
"Le dices cuatro cosas desde lejos y los auxiliares te llevan dentro.":"You tell him a few home truths from afar and the stewards take you inside.",
"Le dices que escucharás ofertas.":"You tell him you'll listen to offers.",
"Le dices que no vas a salir… y en la tanda paras dos. Nadie te recuerda el desplante.":"You tell him you won't come off... and in the shootout you save two. Nobody mentions the snub.",
"Le encierras en la banda hasta que llegan las ayudas.":"You shepherd him toward the touchline until help arrives.",
"Le enseñas la ciudad y las costumbres del vestuario. Os hacéis inseparables.":"You show him the city and the dressing room customs. You become inseparable.",
"Le enseñas lo que a ti te enseñaron. Te sientes bien y el míster lo valora.":"You teach him what you were taught. You feel good and the manager values it.",
"Le explicas que debe ganárselo solo. En casa hay mal ambiente unos días.":"You explain he has to earn it himself. The mood at home is tense for a few days.",
"Le explicas que rindes mejor en tu puesto. Lo acepta, pero toma nota.":"You explain you perform better in your position. He accepts it, but takes note.",
"Le gusta abrir el pie y tirar raso":"Likes to side-foot it low",
"Le gusta tirar fuerte al centro":"Likes to blast it down the middle",
"Le gustas, pero prefiere a otros en tu puesto de momento.":"He likes you, but for now he prefers others in your position.",
"Le han expulsado por protestar. ¿Se arrepiente de su reacción?":"You were sent off for dissent. Do you regret your reaction?",
"Le han multado por sus declaraciones sobre el arbitraje. ¿Se arrepiente?":"You've been fined for your comments on refereeing. Any regrets?",
"Le he pedido más en privado. En público, lo defiendo siempre.":"I've asked more of him in private. In public, I'll always defend him.",
"Le llamas por videollamada.":"You call by video.",
