"Llevas el balón hasta el área y habilitas a una compañera. Gol.":"You carry the ball to the box and set up a teammate. Goal.",
"Llevas meses lejos de tu país. El clima, la comida y la soledad empiezan a pesarte y lo notas en el campo.":"You've been away from your country for months. The weather, the food and the loneliness are starting to get to you and it shows on the pitch.",
"Llevas meses pensando en tatuarte el brazo entero con el escudo de tu ciudad.":"You've been thinking for months about getting your whole arm tattooed with your city's crest.",
"Llevas semanas de baja ({injury}) y aún quedan meses. Se acerca una cita muy importante y todos preguntan cuándo vuelves.":"You've been out for weeks ({injury}) and there are still months to go. A huge occasion is coming up and everyone is asking when you'll be back.",
"Llevas semanas sin disfrutar. Te cuesta dormir y el fútbol pesa más de lo normal.":"You haven't been enjoying yourself for weeks. You struggle to sleep and football weighs more than usual.",
"Llevas semanas sin jugar y con la sensación de que el míster te ignora. Perdéis por dos goles a falta de quince minutos y te manda calentar.":"You haven't played for weeks and feel the manager is ignoring you. You're two goals down with fifteen minutes left and he tells you to warm up.",
