"Te han puesto un mote que escuece: «{nick}»":"You've been given a nickname that stings: “{nick}”",
"Te has convertido en meme":"You've become a meme",
"Te invitan a un partido benéfico para recaudar fondos para familias sin recursos. Es en tu día libre y el club no lo ve con buenos ojos por el riesgo de lesión.":"You're invited to a charity match to raise money for families in need. It's on your day off and the club frowns on it because of the injury risk.",
"Te irás libre en verano. Al club no le gustará.":"You'll leave for free in the summer. The club won't like it.",
"Te la da, pero los nervios te juegan una mala pasada.":"He gives it to you, but nerves get the better of you.",
"Te la roban y gol. El míster se lleva las manos a la cabeza.":"They steal it and score. The manager puts his hands on his head.",
"Te lanzan de todo, el partido se para y acabas fuera de ti. Tu peor tarde.":"They throw everything at you, the game stops and you lose it. Your worst afternoon.",
"Te llaman sobrevalorado":"They call you overrated",
